<title>USA: NACCO gains 10 pct after stock repurchase plan.</title>
<headline>NACCO gains 10 pct after stock repurchase plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of NACCO Industries Inc climbed over ten percent on Monday after the company announced it would start a Dutch auction tender offer to buyback up to 800,000 shares of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The shares rose 4-1/2 to 47-3/4. The Mayfield Heights, Ohio company said late Friday it would buy the shares back for between $43.50 and $50 each.</p>
<p>The company had about 8.9 million primary shares outstanding at the end of the third quarter.</p>
<p>NACCO makes forklift trucks, sells lignite coal, and makes the Hamilton Beach an Procter Silex lines of kitchen appliances.</p>
